1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:01,960
Let's part ways.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,000
I don't think I can do this anymore.

3
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:07,200
<i>If someone betrayed you,</i>
<i>what would you do?</i>

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:09,880
<i>You keep forgiving people.</i>
<i>When are you ever going to get revenge?</i>

5
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:12,560
<i>A presto amora!</i>

6
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:13,840
<i>Wait.</i>

7
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,040
<i>Why do you have this pen?</i>

8
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:16,160
This pen?

9
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:17,920
Well, it's mine.

10
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,360
Rin!

11
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:26,600
You're still alive.

12
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:34,840
Here.

13
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:39,200
Thanks.

14
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:45,240
So now are you going to tell me
why you suddenly showed up like that?

15
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:55,920
I thought you'd been run over, you know?

16
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,480
Me?

17
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:00,640
Weren't you the one who almost got hit?

18
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:10,560
But nothing else unlucky
happened to you today, right?

19
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,840
Today? Not really.

20
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,320
I just fell over a little this morning.

21
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:21,080
My motorcycle ran out of gas,

22
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:22,720
and someone spilled orange juice
all over my shirt.

23
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:24,160
It was a damn mess.

24
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:25,600
That's why I had to change into this.

25
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:27,040
That's all.

26
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:31,120
Yeah, exactly.
Everything that happened was unlucky.

27
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:34,200
Hey. Do you want to go make merit with me?

28
00:01:34,280 --> 00:01:35,640
Come on. Let me take you.

29
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:37,800
No.

30
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:39,960
I don't care about that stuff.

31
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:00,280
<i>Huh? What?</i>

32
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:03,080
The heir to our family's mystical lineage?

33
00:02:08,039 --> 00:02:09,759
Hello, Grandma.

34
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:11,680
Do you know where Mom is?

35
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:14,840
"Mom"? Whose mom? My mom?

36
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:17,360
Oh, my mom died ages ago!

37
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:20,400
No, I mean my mom, Grandma.

38
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:21,960
It's Rin, your grandson.

39
00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:23,840
Rin? Which Rin?

40
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:24,880
I don't know you!

41
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:25,920
It's this, Grandma.

42
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,320
How do you break a curse
and stop someone from having bad luck?

43
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:30,400
A crash? What is it?

44
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:32,720
Not a crash, Grandma.
A curse! Curse, Grandma!

45
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:34,600
What? Say it again.

46
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:36,840
A curse.
Like cursing someone with bad luck.

47
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:39,640
A crash?
I don't know what you're talking about.

48
00:02:39,720 --> 00:02:41,560
A curse, Grandma, not a crash!

49
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:44,440
Crash this, crash that…
I don't know. I'm done talking.

50
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:45,520
Grandma!

51
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:47,240
Hey, Grandma?

52
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:50,840
What the heck?

53
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:53,040
Why are you yelling so loudly?

54
00:02:56,320 --> 00:02:57,800
Oh right.

55
00:02:57,880 --> 00:03:00,000
Did you accidentally throw away
this spellbook the other day?

56
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:02,920
I found it, so I brought it back for you.

57
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:07,160
Say thank you, little Rin!

58
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:10,000
- You little bastard!
- Why?

59
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:11,440
No. It won't get me.

60
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:14,080
- It won't.
- Damn you!

61
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:16,960
If you're upset, don't take it out on me.

62
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:20,000
It's all your fault, you little shit!

63
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:21,520
Don't use my bathroom again!

64
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:44,560
IF THE CURSE IS NOT BROKEN
BEFORE THE CURSED PERSON'S BIRTHDAY,

65
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:46,200
THAT PERSON WILL MEET THEIR END

66
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:51,120
<i>How the hell am I supposed to know</i>
<i>when his birthday is?</i>

67
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:03,000
Hey.

68
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:07,320
I'm from the Faculty of Education.
I'm currently conducting some research.

69
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:10,000
Could you fill out a questionnaire for me?

70
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:11,960
I'm sorry. I'm really busy.

71
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:14,400
Okay. No problem.

72
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:19,240
Hey, wait.

73
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:21,040
Could I take one copy
of the questionnaire?

74
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:23,280
- I'll ask my friend to fill it out.
- Really?

75
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:29,160
Once you've got the answers,
you can email them to me.

76
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:33,600
Oh, and this is a little reward
for completing the questionnaire.

77
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:34,840
Okay.

78
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:39,000
Hello?

79
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:42,760
Hey, calm down.
I'm working on it right now. I'm doing it.

80
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:43,920
Relax, okay?

81
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,640
Tell the professor it'll be
finished on time. It won't be late.

82
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:48,960
Oh, Khobfa?

83
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:52,000
Perfect. You're here.

84
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:53,680
Help me fill out this questionnaire.

85
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:55,440
I have to submit it this evening.

86
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:57,400
Please.

87
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:00,400
What questionnaire is this?

88
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,600
You want to know?
Come on. Let's get started.

89
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:06,840
Mr. Khobfa.

90
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:10,040
How old are you? 20 or 21?

91
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:11,760
I'm 20. I'm not 21 yet.

92
00:06:11,840 --> 00:06:14,040
So your birthday hasn't passed yet.

93
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,280
What's your date of birth?

94
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:19,240
Why do you need to know that?

95
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:22,360
It's a personal identification question.

96
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:23,920
Hurry up.

97
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:26,160
August 20th.

98
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:27,160
What year?

99
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:28,720
2005.

100
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:31,120
Okay. What time were you born?

101
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:32,760
What does that mean?

102
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:34,480
Your exact time of birth.

103
00:06:35,440 --> 00:06:38,240
What kind of questionnaire
asks for your time of birth?

104
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,480
Just answer me.

105
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:44,560
2:30 p.m.

106
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:47,680
2:30 p.m.

107
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:49,040
Okay.

108
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,920
Is that the whole questionnaire?

109
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,560
Those were only the basic questions.

110
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:02,640
Oh right. Yeah. I completely forgot.

111
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:05,320
Let's keep going.

112
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:09,720
Okay. First question.

113
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:12,360
At what age did you first have sex?

114
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:13,440
What?

115
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:18,040
Why are you so shocked?

116
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:20,560
It's just a basic question.

117
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:22,400
Answer it. Don't think too much.

118
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:25,000
Can I ask you the same thing?

119
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:27,440
At what age did you first have sex?

120
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:33,320
If you tell me, I'll tell you mine.

121
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:38,040
Hurry up. It's only a basic question.

122
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:40,040
It shouldn't be difficult
to answer, should it?

123
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:45,120
I've never done it.

124
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:46,800
Jeez.

125
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:51,560
Well, now it's your turn.

126
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,480
Never.

127
00:07:58,440 --> 00:08:00,680
What's with that look on your face?

128
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:03,200
Just write it down.

129
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:04,640
"Never."

130
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:11,760
Can I believe you?

131
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:15,120
One hundred percent.

132
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:22,480
Okay.

133
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:28,480
Oh, I almost forgot.

134
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:31,400
Your reward
for completing the questionnaire.

135
00:08:33,559 --> 00:08:34,720
- Shit!
- Shit!

136
00:08:37,679 --> 00:08:40,200
You haven't done it yet,
but you will someday.

137
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:41,760
Keep it for later.

138
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:06,280
His birthday is in three months.

139
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:10,400
What am I supposed to do next?

140
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:19,960
There are witches too?

141
00:09:24,920 --> 00:09:27,320
Damn, this stuff is scary.

142
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,760
HOW TO BREAK A CURSE

143
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:43,080
10 WAYS TO BREAK
BLACK MAGIC AND DARK SPELLS

144
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:44,440
BREAKING THE "CURSED FATE"

145
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:47,800
Why are there so many?

146
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:56,680
AI, could you summarize which method
of breaking a curse works best?

147
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:59,800
<i>Certainly.</i>
<i>It depends on what you believe in.</i>

148
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:02,080
<i>Many different methods</i>
<i>are commonly discussed</i>

149
00:10:02,160 --> 00:10:06,440
<i>in online communities related</i>
<i>to spiritual beliefs and superstition.</i>

150
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:10,640
Then could you give me
the most reliable one?

151
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:17,840
<i>I recommend MUNIVERSE on OpenChat.</i>

152
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:23,200
<i>It has tens of thousands of members</i>
<i>and a reliability rating of 98.9%.</i>

153
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:28,720
MUNIVERSE?

154
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:46,960
WHY DID YOU JOIN MUNIVERSE?

155
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:48,720
<i>I'm looking for a way to break a curse.</i>

156
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:58,080
<i>I found my cat</i>
<i>after it had been missing for days.</i>

157
00:10:58,160 --> 00:10:59,680
<i>Thank you so much, everyone,</i>

158
00:10:59,760 --> 00:11:02,680
<i>for suggesting that I use</i>
<i>Khaitoon's photo to make a wish.</i>

159
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:05,880
<i>You're welcome. I'm so happy for you.</i>

160
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:17,040
<i>If we accidentally cursed someone</i>
<i>and caused them to have bad luck,</i>

161
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:19,400
<i>what should we do</i>
<i>to make their bad luck disappear?</i>

162
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:25,040
<i>Take the person to a ritual</i>
<i>to ward off their bad luck.</i>

163
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:35,040
<i>Is there another way?</i>

164
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:37,280
<i>I don't think he'd ever agree</i>
<i>to go with me.</i>

165
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:47,120
<i>Then try using his photo</i>
<i>to pray to something sacred instead.</i>

166
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:53,240
A photo?

167
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:13,600
He's secretly stalking a guy.

168
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:15,400
Yeah, he's so boy crazy.

169
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:19,160
Hey, wait. No, that's not it!

170
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:21,240
Isn't this a PDPA violation?

171
00:12:29,400 --> 00:12:30,480
Huh?

172
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:32,640
Damn it.

173
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:43,320
YOUNG ENTREPRENEURS

174
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:18,200
So you're the one who played that guitar?

175
00:13:50,880 --> 00:13:53,960
Hey, what the hell are you doing?

176
00:13:57,920 --> 00:13:59,600
Well…

177
00:13:59,680 --> 00:14:02,680
I'm taking pictures of flowers. I have
to sketch and submit it to my professor.

178
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:09,320
Fake flowers?

179
00:14:10,760 --> 00:14:13,480
Fake flowers are still flowers anyway.

180
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:14,680
Really?

181
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:18,880
I got the pictures. I'm leaving.

182
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:31,080
Let me make a wish.
Khobfa, the person in this photo…

183
00:14:31,160 --> 00:14:34,520
Please keep him safe.
Let only good things happen to him.

184
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:37,280
Don't let him experience
any more bad luck.

185
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:39,240
Please make the curse of bad luck
I placed on him…

186
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:43,080
disappear!

187
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:57,800
<i>I've already tried using his photo</i>
<i>to pray to something sacred.</i>

188
00:14:57,880 --> 00:15:00,320
<i>All right.</i>
<i>Let's wait and see what happens.</i>

189
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:01,800
<i>Good luck.</i>

190
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:06,840
Sacred spirits, sacred spirits,
please help me.

191
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:12,480
- My dear friend Rin.
- Yes?

192
00:15:12,560 --> 00:15:14,960
Do you want to go
to the movies with us tomorrow?

193
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:18,400
After the movie, how about karaoke?

194
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:22,320
<i>- Love, love, I need somebody to love</i>
<i>- Love, love, I need somebody to love</i>

195
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:25,160
Well, I really want to go with you guys,

196
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:28,280
but I have something to take care of.

197
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:30,080
Maybe next time.

198
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:33,720
You're always like this.

199
00:15:35,160 --> 00:15:39,480
Come on. Once I finish dealing with this,
I will get my freedom back.

200
00:15:40,680 --> 00:15:42,360
What are you dealing with?

201
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:46,360
Well, I have to…

202
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:50,760
<i>- Love, love, I need somebody to love</i>
<i>- I need somebody to love</i>

203
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:55,400
<i>But that person must be you</i>

204
00:15:55,480 --> 00:15:58,480
- Why didn't you continue singing with me?
- I don't know the lyrics.

205
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:16,600
The target is currently safe.

206
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:18,120
I'll continue monitoring him.

207
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:24,760
SOLD OUT!

208
00:16:30,400 --> 00:16:32,240
Is he seriously still having bad luck?

209
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:34,680
<i>That's normal.</i>
<i>I'd recommend waiting a little longer.</i>

210
00:16:34,760 --> 00:16:35,880
Maybe it was just a coincidence.

211
00:16:40,760 --> 00:16:43,800
Shit. I don't think
this is a coincidence anymore.

212
00:16:48,480 --> 00:16:51,720
The target is on the move.
No signs of bad luck.

213
00:16:57,560 --> 00:16:58,880
- Shit!
- I'm sorry.

214
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:00,800
- It's okay. I'm fine.
- Are you okay?

215
00:17:01,800 --> 00:17:03,560
He could've died from that!

216
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,839
<i>It didn't work.</i>

217
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:09,800
<i>I already prayed to something sacred,</i>

218
00:17:09,880 --> 00:17:12,040
<i>but he still keeps having</i>
<i>the same bad luck.</i>

219
00:17:12,119 --> 00:17:14,920
<i>Does anyone know</i>
<i>another method I could try?</i>

220
00:17:16,640 --> 00:17:18,319
<i>Try using holy water.</i>

221
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:19,680
<i>They say that</i>

222
00:17:19,760 --> 00:17:23,119
<i>when someone has been cursed,</i>
<i>you should have them drink holy water.</i>

223
00:17:24,599 --> 00:17:29,120
<i>Holy water will make them</i>
<i>vomit out the evil inside them.</i>

224
00:17:33,560 --> 00:17:37,280
<i>This is holy water from a Buddhist temple,</i>
<i>and this is holy water from a church.</i>

225
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:01,600
Mixing both together has to work!

226
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:24,640
What is Rin doing there?

227
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:26,280
There are plenty of other seats.

228
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:28,240
Why are you sitting here?

229
00:18:28,320 --> 00:18:30,600
Can't I sit with you?

230
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:34,320
Isn't he dating Khobfa just to spite you?

231
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:41,120
Hey, did that person bring a cat to class?

232
00:18:43,360 --> 00:18:45,560
Whoa! That cat is huge.

233
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:55,200
Where's the cat?

234
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:58,280
What the hell is wrong with you?

235
00:19:01,560 --> 00:19:04,000
What are you eating? That looks good.

236
00:19:04,080 --> 00:19:05,200
None of your business.

237
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:23,760
Hey.

238
00:19:24,520 --> 00:19:25,640
Hey, what's wrong?

239
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:27,640
Hey.

240
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:29,240
Spicy?

241
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:34,520
Here. I bought you some water.

242
00:19:59,760 --> 00:20:01,000
I'm not drinking your water.

243
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:10,880
Jeez.

244
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:18,640
What am I supposed to do now?

245
00:20:40,680 --> 00:20:42,240
You don't have to do that
just to spite me.

246
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:45,960
Spite you? How?

247
00:20:46,720 --> 00:20:50,000
Since when did you two get so close?

248
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:52,600
We're in the same class.

249
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:57,960
Khobfa isn't usually your type.

250
00:21:00,560 --> 00:21:02,680
And Krit is totally your type then?

251
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:05,520
Mochi.

252
00:21:14,640 --> 00:21:16,080
If that's all, I'm leaving.

253
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:48,680
I'm sorry about that.

254
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:52,760
Rin hates you because of me.

255
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:09,880
Are you okay?

256
00:22:10,480 --> 00:22:11,480
I'm okay.

257
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:16,000
Did I make other people
think badly of you?

258
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:18,640
I feel guilty.

259
00:22:19,520 --> 00:22:22,640
Forget about it.
I can't blame anyone for thinking that.

260
00:22:27,920 --> 00:22:28,760
Hey, wait.

261
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:41,280
How can you still eat
so messily at your age?

262
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:49,000
How am I supposed to eat this
without making a mess?

263
00:22:54,320 --> 00:22:55,160
Wipe it again.

264
00:22:56,160 --> 00:22:57,440
What are you, a baby?

265
00:22:58,160 --> 00:22:59,440
That sounds pretty cool.

266
00:23:04,040 --> 00:23:06,760
Whoa, didn't you just make it
even messier?

267
00:23:08,680 --> 00:23:10,960
In nature,

268
00:23:11,040 --> 00:23:14,200
every tree has a language of its own,

269
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:18,320
and each tree grows at a different pace.

270
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:22,280
Some trees need a long time
to establish deep roots,

271
00:23:22,360 --> 00:23:24,080
while others need less time.

272
00:23:24,160 --> 00:23:26,720
Do you know that
not every tree can survive?

273
00:23:26,800 --> 00:23:29,920
<i>Do you want to go make merit with me?</i>
<i>Come on. Let me take you.</i>

274
00:23:30,600 --> 00:23:31,600
No.

275
00:23:31,680 --> 00:23:33,400
I don't care about that stuff.

276
00:23:35,120 --> 00:23:36,000
- Shit!
- I'm sorry.

277
00:23:36,080 --> 00:23:37,240
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine.

278
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:45,800
Do you know why it died?

279
00:23:46,440 --> 00:23:49,520
It wasn't an environmental problem
that killed the tree.

280
00:23:49,600 --> 00:23:55,960
It died because the person who planted it
accidentally hurt and killed it.

281
00:23:56,040 --> 00:23:59,040
It's the same with our relationships.

282
00:23:59,800 --> 00:24:05,200
Sometimes, we accidentally leave small,
invisible wounds on other people too.

283
00:24:05,880 --> 00:24:07,440
But the question is,

284
00:24:07,520 --> 00:24:10,960
does the caretaker
who accidentally damaged the branch

285
00:24:11,040 --> 00:24:13,320
still want to continue
taking care of the tree?

286
00:24:14,600 --> 00:24:19,320
Let's go back to the tree
whose branch we accidentally broke.

287
00:24:19,400 --> 00:24:21,480
Do you believe that if the caretaker…

288
00:24:21,560 --> 00:24:24,560
<i>I tried to get him to drink</i>
<i>the holy water, but he wouldn't.</i>

289
00:24:24,640 --> 00:24:26,000
<i>What should I do?</i>

290
00:24:28,760 --> 00:24:32,920
<i>Someone who isn't close to you</i>
<i>probably won't eat anything from you.</i>

291
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:35,120
<i>Try getting closer to them first.</i>

292
00:24:35,200 --> 00:24:37,640
So today, I have an assignment
for all of you.

293
00:24:37,720 --> 00:24:39,920
This time, you'll be working in pairs.

294
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:44,000
Therefore, everyone needs
to pair up today.

295
00:24:44,080 --> 00:24:48,160
You must submit your names to me
by the end of the day. Understood?

296
00:24:48,240 --> 00:24:50,680
- All right.
- Got it.

297
00:24:50,760 --> 00:24:52,640
Let's work together.

298
00:24:52,720 --> 00:24:54,120
Of course.

299
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:57,280
Hey, what should the three of us do?

300
00:24:57,360 --> 00:24:59,040
Should we ask
if we can work as a group of three?

301
00:24:59,120 --> 00:25:00,240
Yeah.

302
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:03,440
- Maybe we should ask him.
- Right.

303
00:25:03,520 --> 00:25:06,720
The person sitting next to me
refused to work with me. Shit.

304
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:08,840
Hey.

305
00:25:10,240 --> 00:25:11,520
Do you see Khobfa?

306
00:25:12,360 --> 00:25:13,920
He just sits there looking miserable.

307
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:17,280
Doesn't he care that
he doesn't have a partner to work with?

308
00:25:18,440 --> 00:25:19,360
That's weird.

309
00:25:21,320 --> 00:25:22,880
Okay, so the three of us
will work together.

310
00:25:22,960 --> 00:25:24,320
- Yeah.
- You come up with the topic.

311
00:25:24,400 --> 00:25:27,960
- Rin can write the report.
<i>- Try getting closer to them first.</i>

312
00:25:28,040 --> 00:25:28,880
Come on.

313
00:25:28,960 --> 00:25:31,800
Actually, I think you two should pair up.
I've got a partner already.

314
00:25:31,880 --> 00:25:33,120
- Huh?
- Huh?

315
00:25:34,480 --> 00:25:35,680
Hey, wait.

316
00:25:35,760 --> 00:25:37,240
- Hey.
- Rin?

317
00:25:37,920 --> 00:25:39,080
What the hell?

318
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:41,720
- Khobfa.
- Shit!

319
00:25:41,800 --> 00:25:43,600
You don't have a partner
for the assignment, right?

320
00:25:43,680 --> 00:25:45,800
Neither do I. Let's pair up.

321
00:25:47,080 --> 00:25:49,080
I'm going to ask the professor
to let me work alone.

322
00:25:51,280 --> 00:25:52,440
Huh?

323
00:25:52,520 --> 00:25:55,560
Wait! Khobfa!

324
00:25:56,320 --> 00:25:58,680
If you work alone,
you might get unlucky again.

325
00:26:00,960 --> 00:26:02,520
I can take care of myself.

326
00:26:03,320 --> 00:26:04,240
Khobfa!

327
00:26:04,320 --> 00:26:06,200
Khobfa, are you okay?

328
00:26:07,240 --> 00:26:08,480
Are you okay?

329
00:26:10,560 --> 00:26:11,880
I'm fine.

330
00:26:12,960 --> 00:26:13,960
Ouch!

331
00:26:14,040 --> 00:26:15,240
Hey, be careful.

332
00:26:25,640 --> 00:26:26,760
Don't push yourself.

333
00:26:26,840 --> 00:26:28,000
Let's go to the infirmary.

334
00:26:30,280 --> 00:26:31,480
Get up.

335
00:26:37,840 --> 00:26:40,080
Walk slowly.

336
00:26:40,160 --> 00:26:42,920
STUDENTS MUST SIGN TO ACKNOWLEDGE RECEIPT
OF MEDICATION AND SERVICES

337
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:44,200
Be careful for now.

338
00:26:44,280 --> 00:26:46,000
Don't walk too quickly,

339
00:26:46,080 --> 00:26:48,760
and apply a cold compress
three or four times a day.

340
00:26:48,840 --> 00:26:50,880
Don't forget to take the medicine
I gave you.

341
00:26:50,960 --> 00:26:52,360
- You'll recover faster.
- Thanks.

342
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:54,000
- Thank you.
- Get well soon.

343
00:26:55,400 --> 00:26:57,400
Come on.

344
00:26:58,600 --> 00:26:59,600
Easy.

345
00:27:03,360 --> 00:27:04,200
Walk slowly.

346
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:07,400
Wait here for now.
I already got you a ride.

347
00:27:08,080 --> 00:27:08,920
Huh?

348
00:27:09,680 --> 00:27:11,240
I'll ride my motorcycle home by myself.

349
00:27:11,320 --> 00:27:13,760
Your leg is injured. How can you ride?

350
00:27:13,840 --> 00:27:15,360
Absolutely not.

351
00:27:16,440 --> 00:27:17,400
It's arriving.

352
00:27:18,480 --> 00:27:19,320
Hey!

353
00:27:34,360 --> 00:27:36,560
No need. I'll open the door for you.

354
00:27:47,400 --> 00:27:48,240
Wait.

355
00:27:49,440 --> 00:27:50,400
What is it again?

356
00:27:50,480 --> 00:27:53,280
I'm going with you. How can you go alone?

357
00:27:53,360 --> 00:27:54,680
Move. Let me sit with you.

358
00:27:57,480 --> 00:27:58,400
Let's go, please.

359
00:28:17,320 --> 00:28:18,800
Take it slowly.

360
00:28:21,320 --> 00:28:23,000
You only need to take me this far.

361
00:28:23,680 --> 00:28:24,680
I can go by myself.

362
00:28:25,360 --> 00:28:27,080
How can you go alone?

363
00:28:27,160 --> 00:28:29,360
I said I can manage.

364
00:28:30,640 --> 00:28:31,640
Ouch.

365
00:28:31,720 --> 00:28:33,240
See?

366
00:28:42,920 --> 00:28:44,880
You never listen to me. See?

367
00:28:44,960 --> 00:28:46,720
Let me take you to your room.

368
00:28:49,560 --> 00:28:50,400
Come on.

369
00:28:52,760 --> 00:28:55,480
Don't put too much weight on it yet.
It won't get better if you do.

370
00:28:58,200 --> 00:28:59,520
You can manage, right?

371
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:00,880
Yeah.

372
00:29:04,120 --> 00:29:05,600
Don't forget to apply
a cold compress often,

373
00:29:05,680 --> 00:29:06,720
and don't walk too much.

374
00:29:07,400 --> 00:29:11,120
Also, don't forget to take the painkillers
the nurse gave you. Got it?

375
00:29:14,640 --> 00:29:15,920
Oh.

376
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:18,000
I ran out of water.

377
00:29:18,080 --> 00:29:19,760
Can I have some of yours?

378
00:29:26,840 --> 00:29:27,720
But…

379
00:29:27,800 --> 00:29:31,280
I've already drunk from this bottle.

380
00:29:31,360 --> 00:29:32,920
I don't mind.

381
00:30:01,480 --> 00:30:02,920
I'll…

382
00:30:03,960 --> 00:30:05,440
I'll do the report with you.

383
00:30:13,160 --> 00:30:14,000
Khobfa.

384
00:30:16,360 --> 00:30:17,200
Yeah?

385
00:30:17,880 --> 00:30:18,760
See you tomorrow.

386
00:30:20,320 --> 00:30:21,760
Get well soon.

387
00:30:45,600 --> 00:30:47,800
Yes!

388
00:30:47,880 --> 00:30:50,600
You drank the holy water.
Your bad luck will finally gone!

389
00:30:53,240 --> 00:30:54,880
This one is mine.

390
00:30:54,960 --> 00:30:56,400
I'll remember that.

391
00:30:59,440 --> 00:31:00,920
Hey.

392
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:02,160
Rin.

393
00:31:10,640 --> 00:31:11,760
What's wrong with you?

394
00:31:12,520 --> 00:31:13,360
Nothing.

395
00:31:13,440 --> 00:31:15,760
Do you want to eat with us?
We bought a lot.

396
00:31:15,840 --> 00:31:18,120
- Yeah.
- You guys go ahead. I'm full.

397
00:31:19,360 --> 00:31:21,160
You already ate?

398
00:31:21,240 --> 00:31:22,160
Not yet.

399
00:31:23,440 --> 00:31:25,680
My heart is full.

400
00:31:26,640 --> 00:31:27,480
I'm going now.

401
00:31:28,160 --> 00:31:30,880
<i>You're such a darling</i>

402
00:31:30,960 --> 00:31:33,560
<i>You're not even trying</i>

403
00:31:33,640 --> 00:31:35,600
- His heart is full?
- Right.

404
00:31:39,880 --> 00:31:41,520
You're actually pretty cute.

405
00:31:43,320 --> 00:31:45,240
But you complain a little too much.

406
00:32:01,680 --> 00:32:03,320
<i>He drank the holy water.</i>

407
00:32:03,400 --> 00:32:05,200
<i>I think his bad luck is gone now.</i>

408
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:14,880
I hope your bad luck is finally over.

409
00:32:40,120 --> 00:32:41,640
Krit, are you almost done?

410
00:32:41,720 --> 00:32:43,960
It's nearly time
for the live stream we announced.

411
00:32:44,760 --> 00:32:46,680
Give me a second. I'm almost done.

412
00:32:46,760 --> 00:32:47,960
Yeah.

413
00:32:53,440 --> 00:32:54,280
It's done.

414
00:32:57,080 --> 00:32:58,440
Come on. Let's go live.

415
00:33:15,200 --> 00:33:17,520
Your face is oily,
and your hair is a mess.

416
00:33:17,600 --> 00:33:18,800
Come. I'll fix it for you.

417
00:33:48,440 --> 00:33:51,480
What is it?

418
00:33:53,880 --> 00:33:54,720
Nothing.

419
00:33:56,040 --> 00:33:57,280
I like your eyes.

420
00:33:58,200 --> 00:33:59,440
They're pretty.

421
00:34:11,840 --> 00:34:13,400
Thanks.

422
00:34:15,480 --> 00:34:17,199
It's been a long time since anyone

423
00:34:17,840 --> 00:34:21,040
paid attention
to the little things about me.

424
00:34:44,400 --> 00:34:45,840
It's time to go live.

425
00:34:46,560 --> 00:34:48,560
- Let's do it.
- Yeah.

426
00:35:20,760 --> 00:35:22,720
RIN

427
00:35:30,200 --> 00:35:31,040
<i>Hello?</i>

428
00:35:31,720 --> 00:35:32,680
Are you awake?

429
00:35:34,120 --> 00:35:35,040
I'm awake.

430
00:35:36,440 --> 00:35:37,840
See you at the university today.

431
00:35:37,920 --> 00:35:39,760
We're meeting to work on the report.
Did you forget?

432
00:35:40,520 --> 00:35:41,640
No, I didn't.

433
00:35:41,720 --> 00:35:44,160
Do you want me to pick you up?

434
00:35:44,240 --> 00:35:46,920
No need. I'll take a car there myself.

435
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:47,920
<i>Okay.</i>

436
00:35:48,600 --> 00:35:49,800
Be safe.

437
00:36:04,280 --> 00:36:05,240
Hello, Khobfa?

438
00:36:05,320 --> 00:36:06,480
Are you coming out yet?

439
00:36:06,560 --> 00:36:08,640
Yeah. I'm on my way.

440
00:36:11,280 --> 00:36:12,120
Hey!

441
00:36:13,200 --> 00:36:14,480
Khobfa!

442
00:36:14,560 --> 00:36:16,000
What's wrong, Khobfa?

443
00:36:19,400 --> 00:36:20,520
Hey!

444
00:36:21,480 --> 00:36:22,640
Shit.

445
00:36:22,720 --> 00:36:23,920
Rin. What?

446
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:25,200
Rin!

447
00:36:25,280 --> 00:36:26,680
Where are you going?

448
00:36:35,360 --> 00:36:36,680
Khobfa!

449
00:36:42,600 --> 00:36:43,680
What happened?

450
00:36:44,960 --> 00:36:46,320
I'm sorry.

451
00:36:47,480 --> 00:36:51,480
I fell this morning,
so I went to buy some medicine.

452
00:36:53,400 --> 00:36:55,760
I should've picked you up from the start.

453
00:36:56,920 --> 00:36:58,280
It's okay.

454
00:36:59,280 --> 00:37:00,920
I'm not going to class today.

455
00:37:02,240 --> 00:37:04,920
Aren't you going to class?

456
00:37:06,800 --> 00:37:07,920
Forget it.

457
00:37:09,400 --> 00:37:10,920
Are you going straight to your room?

458
00:37:11,520 --> 00:37:14,600
Yeah. I'll head inside now.

459
00:37:20,520 --> 00:37:21,880
Give it to me. I'll help you.

460
00:37:41,360 --> 00:37:42,200
It's open.

461
00:37:59,680 --> 00:38:03,040
Why is it so hard to make one person
stop having bad luck?

462
00:38:03,960 --> 00:38:05,080
<i>Please calm down.</i>

463
00:38:05,160 --> 00:38:07,640
<i>It's normal for people</i>
<i>to go through periods of bad luck.</i>

464
00:38:07,720 --> 00:38:10,640
<i>Before long, the bad things</i>
<i>should pass on their own.</i>

465
00:38:10,720 --> 00:38:12,040
Yeah, that's true.

466
00:38:13,480 --> 00:38:16,200
I'll forget about it then.
I'll just pretend I have.

467
00:38:16,280 --> 00:38:17,600
No one will ever know.

468
00:38:18,280 --> 00:38:19,200
Know what?

469
00:38:20,280 --> 00:38:22,080
Were you talking to me just now?

470
00:38:22,160 --> 00:38:23,360
No.

471
00:38:23,440 --> 00:38:25,640
If there's anything I can help you with,

472
00:38:25,720 --> 00:38:27,720
just tell me.

473
00:38:27,800 --> 00:38:31,960
But today,
something really infuriating happened.

474
00:38:32,040 --> 00:38:34,840
Someone sent people to attack my friend,

475
00:38:34,920 --> 00:38:36,200
but they attacked the wrong person.

476
00:38:36,280 --> 00:38:38,200
- What?
- My friend got hurt for nothing.

477
00:38:38,280 --> 00:38:39,920
So how would you handle it?

478
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:41,480
There was nothing I could do.

479
00:38:41,560 --> 00:38:44,720
As soon as they realized
the truth was out, they ran away.

480
00:38:44,800 --> 00:38:46,240
They're fucking awful.

481
00:38:46,320 --> 00:38:49,560
Yeah, now that you mention it,
that was really stupid of them.

482
00:38:49,640 --> 00:38:51,240
- Yeah.
- They even dragged others.

483
00:38:51,320 --> 00:38:52,800
How is your friend now?

484
00:38:52,880 --> 00:38:55,000
My friend isn't badly hurt.

485
00:38:55,080 --> 00:38:56,640
I'm just angry

486
00:38:56,720 --> 00:38:59,040
that they refuse to take responsibility.

487
00:38:59,120 --> 00:39:00,760
Don't you think they're assholes, Rin?

488
00:39:01,880 --> 00:39:03,400
They're assholes, right?

489
00:39:04,280 --> 00:39:06,320
Yeah. They're complete fucking assholes.

490
00:39:06,400 --> 00:39:08,000
They're the worst.

491
00:39:10,440 --> 00:39:12,200
When you do something wrong,
take responsibility.

492
00:39:12,280 --> 00:39:13,120
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

493
00:39:13,920 --> 00:39:14,920
- Assholes!
- Assholes!

494
00:39:15,000 --> 00:39:17,160
- Total assholes.
- Seriously.

495
00:39:17,240 --> 00:39:19,960
If I were you,
I'd go slap the hell out of them.

496
00:39:20,040 --> 00:39:22,720
I'd slap them left and right.

497
00:39:22,800 --> 00:39:24,600
I'd slap them from the front
and from behind for you.

498
00:39:24,680 --> 00:39:26,080
Let's go right now, okay?

499
00:39:26,160 --> 00:39:28,960
- Whatever you decide, I'm with you.
- I can't take it anymore.

500
00:39:29,040 --> 00:39:29,960
Let's go.

501
00:39:30,040 --> 00:39:31,840
MISSION: SAVE THE UNLUCKY ONE

502
00:39:31,920 --> 00:39:33,680
PHOTO
HOLY WATER

503
00:39:33,760 --> 00:39:35,400
These two methods didn't work.

504
00:39:36,400 --> 00:39:37,720
What the hell should I do now?

505
00:39:55,960 --> 00:39:57,360
A CURSE THAT LEADS TO ONE'S DOOM

506
00:40:00,920 --> 00:40:02,800
This is even worse
than cursing someone with bad luck.

507
00:40:03,400 --> 00:40:05,640
What the hell is this?

508
00:40:08,680 --> 00:40:10,280
MS. DARAN

509
00:40:14,800 --> 00:40:16,200
Mom!

510
00:40:16,280 --> 00:40:17,280
Mom.

511
00:40:17,960 --> 00:40:19,560
What are you doing, sweetheart?

512
00:40:19,640 --> 00:40:22,000
We haven't talked in ages.

513
00:40:22,520 --> 00:40:25,560
I just got a signal. How have you been?

514
00:40:25,640 --> 00:40:27,080
Mom.

515
00:40:27,160 --> 00:40:30,320
But what if I accidentally
used a curse from the spellbook

516
00:40:30,400 --> 00:40:31,800
to bring someone bad luck,

517
00:40:32,320 --> 00:40:34,080
but I don't know how to undo it?

518
00:40:34,160 --> 00:40:35,400
What should I do, Mom?

519
00:40:35,480 --> 00:40:37,360
Did you accidentally curse someone, Rin?

520
00:40:39,080 --> 00:40:40,960
Well, hypothetically, Mom.

521
00:40:41,760 --> 00:40:43,200
I didn't curse anyone.

522
00:40:43,280 --> 00:40:45,240
I'm just curious.

523
00:40:45,320 --> 00:40:49,480
I've never heard of a curse
that has absolutely no solution.

524
00:40:51,320 --> 00:40:54,560
Where there is white,
there must also be black.

525
00:40:55,600 --> 00:40:58,080
If there is night, there must also be day.

526
00:40:59,880 --> 00:41:01,920
I believe everything has a way out.

527
00:41:02,000 --> 00:41:04,680
You just haven't found it yet, Rin.

528
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:10,200
But let me warn you.

529
00:41:10,280 --> 00:41:13,720
The stronger these things are,
the more careful you need to be.

530
00:41:13,800 --> 00:41:17,640
Don't use them recklessly
when you don't truly understand them.

531
00:41:20,680 --> 00:41:21,680
Got it.

532
00:41:22,720 --> 00:41:27,520
But did you accidentally curse someone?

533
00:41:29,000 --> 00:41:30,000
I didn't.

534
00:41:30,080 --> 00:41:31,360
That's all for now, Mom.

535
00:41:43,320 --> 00:41:45,080
Haven't found it?

536
00:41:56,080 --> 00:41:58,320
"Methods to balance misfortune."

537
00:42:02,960 --> 00:42:04,600
"If there be one cursed by misfortune,

538
00:42:05,160 --> 00:42:06,880
then must another of good fortune
be sought out."

539
00:42:08,800 --> 00:42:10,440
"The one of fortune

540
00:42:10,520 --> 00:42:12,880
must be born on the fifteenth waxing moon
of the sixth month,

541
00:42:14,480 --> 00:42:16,120
with the moon
as their ruling celestial body."

542
00:42:18,520 --> 00:42:20,280
Where do I find someone like that?

543
00:42:25,960 --> 00:42:28,600
AI, help me check my birth chart.

544
00:42:28,680 --> 00:42:31,640
I was born on May 17th, 2005.

545
00:42:31,720 --> 00:42:34,880
<i>You were born on the fifteenth night</i>
<i>of the sixth lunar month.</i>

546
00:42:34,960 --> 00:42:37,640
<i>Your ruling celestial body is the moon.</i>

547
00:42:37,720 --> 00:42:38,560
Yes!

548
00:42:39,160 --> 00:42:40,280
Finally!

549
00:42:40,360 --> 00:42:42,280
<i>Are you happy?</i>

550
00:42:42,360 --> 00:42:44,240
Yeah, I am.

551
00:42:44,320 --> 00:42:47,400
At least I'll finally be able
to save someone.

552
00:43:09,160 --> 00:43:10,720
Who's there?

553
00:43:21,240 --> 00:43:22,080
Who is it?

554
00:43:22,160 --> 00:43:24,520
- Yo, bro!
- Shit!

555
00:43:24,600 --> 00:43:25,800
Where did you come from?

556
00:43:25,880 --> 00:43:27,960
I've got good news for you.

557
00:43:28,040 --> 00:43:30,240
To make sure our report goes well

558
00:43:30,320 --> 00:43:32,280
and to keep you from getting hurt,

559
00:43:32,360 --> 00:43:36,040
from now on,
I'll pick you up for university every day.

560
00:43:37,160 --> 00:43:38,480
- Deal, okay?
- Hey!

561
00:43:59,120 --> 00:44:00,000
- Shit!
- Shit!

562
00:44:14,640 --> 00:44:16,560
<i>What am I supposed to do?</i>
<i>I can't be with him.</i>

563
00:44:16,640 --> 00:44:18,960
<i>I'm scared something unlucky</i>
<i>will happen to him again.</i>

564
00:44:19,040 --> 00:44:21,360
<i>Then you'll have to find a way</i>
<i>to stay with him 24 hours a day.</i>

565
00:44:21,440 --> 00:44:23,840
- Let me be your roommate, Khobfa.
- What?

566
00:44:23,920 --> 00:44:27,680
<i>If you make one shot out of five,</i>
<i>I'll let you be my roommate.</i>

567
00:44:27,760 --> 00:44:29,160
<i>You have to shoot with your eyes closed.</i>

568
00:44:29,240 --> 00:44:33,760
<i>I know you're busy,</i>
<i>but don't forget my birthday party.</i>

569
00:44:33,840 --> 00:44:36,720
It's not because I've met someone new.
You and I just can't be together anymore.

570
00:44:36,800 --> 00:44:38,080
<i>You've got it all wrong.</i>

571
00:44:38,160 --> 00:44:39,640
<i>Rin didn't come here to see you.</i>

572
00:44:39,720 --> 00:44:40,760
He came to see me.
